-- The comma rule of §2.3 is the `where` clause's TOP LEVEL and nothing
-- else: inside a record type the comma separates FIELDS, under the record
-- rule of language.md §3. `b.c` is not a field name, so this file is
-- broken either way — what it pins is which rule owned the comma. With the
-- constraint rule leaking into the braces the comma ended the field and
-- `b` became the next field; with it confined to the clause, the field's
-- type runs on and the `.c` that cannot continue a type is the error.
-- where_variable_unbound at 10:28, expected_token at 10:29.
pub render : a → Int
    where a.m : { x : Int, b.c : Int } → Int
render v =
    1
